WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.760
What if someone who already has the keys
takes what we cannot afford to lose?

00:00:05.090 --> 00:00:07.960
Insider threat comes in
four kinds of people.

00:00:09.250 --> 00:00:10.380
First, the leaver.

00:00:10.745 --> 00:00:14.655
In the notice period,
a salesperson exports the customer list.

00:00:14.970 --> 00:00:17.740
Access stays fully open
until the last day.

00:00:17.970 --> 00:00:21.920
The export looks like normal work,
and the damage shows months later.

00:00:22.983 --> 00:00:24.953
Second, the colleague who meant well.

00:00:25.218 --> 00:00:29.588
Autocomplete picks the wrong address,
and a salary overview goes outside.

00:00:29.923 --> 00:00:32.573
Or a folder is shared
with anyone with the link.

00:00:32.878 --> 00:00:37.208
Nobody wanted harm, but it is the
same breach, with the same regulator.

00:00:38.383 --> 00:00:40.753
Third, the administrator nobody reviews.

00:00:41.198 --> 00:00:43.548
One person can export
the customer database,

00:00:43.938 --> 00:00:46.608
create a spare account and clear the log.

00:00:46.873 --> 00:00:48.503
Then no evidence is left.

00:00:49.583 --> 00:00:51.573
Fourth, the employee under pressure.

00:00:51.858 --> 00:00:54.468
Criminals offer a few
thousand for a login.

00:00:54.788 --> 00:00:56.658
Others are pushed with debt or threats.

00:00:57.053 --> 00:01:01.583
A trusted account doing untrusted
things is the hardest attack to detect.

00:01:02.683 --> 00:01:03.893
What good looks like.

00:01:04.238 --> 00:01:07.348
NIS2 Article 21 names access control,

00:01:07.758 --> 00:01:10.408
human resources security
and asset management.

00:01:10.788 --> 00:01:13.578
That means access limited
to what the job needs,

00:01:14.088 --> 00:01:16.538
access that shrinks when notice is given,

00:01:16.968 --> 00:01:19.288
a second person approving
privileged actions,

00:01:19.288 --> 00:01:22.658
and logs that administrators cannot erase.

00:01:23.073 --> 00:01:25.543
Staff should feel safe to
report being approached.

00:01:27.430 --> 00:01:28.640
A suggested first step.

00:01:28.925 --> 00:01:33.395
Ask which five datasets would hurt most
if one person walked out with them.

00:01:33.595 --> 00:01:36.505
Then ask how many people
can reach each one today.

00:01:36.775 --> 00:01:40.945
If nobody knows, that is the whole
insider programme in one line.

00:01:42.450 --> 00:01:44.040
Trust is not a control.

00:01:44.435 --> 00:01:47.045
Limit access,
and keep the evidence complete.

